### API Test Collection
### Save this file as test-api.http and use REST Client extension in VS Code

### Test 1: Check if API is running
GET http://localhost:5000

###

### Test 2: Register a new user
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "John Doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Test 3: Register a seller
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jane Seller",
  "email": "jane.seller@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "seller",
  "storeName": "Jane's Store",
  "storeDescription": "Quality products for everyone"
}

###

### Test 4: Login
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### Test 5: Get current user (Replace YOUR_TOKEN_HERE with actual token from login)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

###

### Test 6: Update password
PUT http://localhost:5000/api/auth/updatepassword
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "password123",
  "newPassword": "newpassword123"
}

###

### Test 7: Logout
POST http://localhost:5000/api/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

###

### Test 8: Admin route (will fail without admin role)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/admin/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE

###

### Test 9: Seller route (will fail if seller not approved)
GET http://localhost:5000/api/seller/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
